@ SOFiSTiK 2026
$ A SOFiSTiK input sample, kept idiomatic so it is worth opening in the editor.
$ Each PROG block is scoped by the module it runs, and a $ starts a comment.

+PROG AQUA urs:1
HEAD Materials and cross sections
PAGE UNII 0

NORM DIN EN1992-2004
CONC 1 C 30 TITL 'C30/37'
STEE 2 B 500 TITL 'B500B'

SREC 1 H 0.60 B 0.30 MNO 1 MRF 2 TITL 'Beam 300/600'
END

+PROG SOFIMSHA urs:2
HEAD Geometry
SYST 3D GDIR NEGZ

NODE 1 X 0.00 Y 0 Z 0 FIX PP
NODE 2 X 6.00 Y 0 Z 0 FIX PZ
NODE 3 X 12.00 Y 0 Z 0 FIX PZ

BEAM 1 NA 1 NE 2 NCS 1 DIV 6
BEAM 2 NA 2 NE 3 NCS 1 DIV 6
END

+PROG SOFILOAD urs:3
HEAD Loads

LC 1 TYPE G TITL 'Self weight'
  LCC 1 DLZ 1.0

LC 2 TYPE Q TITL 'Live load'
  LINE TYPE PZ P1 -10.0 REF S FROM 0.0 TO 1.0

END

+PROG ASE urs:4
HEAD Linear analysis
CTRL SOLV 4
LC 1,2
END

$ A disabled block keeps its highlighting but is not run.
-PROG BEMESS urs:5
HEAD Design
END

+PROG WING urs:6
HEAD Results
GRA ; SIZE URS 6
STRU ; BEAM STYP 'M-Y'
END
